Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.70,0:00:02.83,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}This is Brindle Cross.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.91,0:00:09.00,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}The clock runs slow.\NThirty-one minutes, at last count.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.54,0:00:12.12,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Nobody’s quite sure\Nwhen that started.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.62,0:00:16.16,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Somebody kept eating\Nthe rye before he’d paid.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.25,0:00:18.00,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Hence, the sign.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.08,0:00:20.16,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}This is Tomas Brandt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.70,0:00:23.58,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}This is his son, Teddy. He is eight.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.25,0:00:28.00,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Teddy. Door.\NYou’re letting the heat out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.33,0:00:31.79,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}The lamp lights itself at five.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.33,0:00:35.79,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}And this is Oswald Bunce.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.83,0:00:39.62,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}It’s a silent act.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.00,0:00:56.62,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Again!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.62,0:00:57.91,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Door!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.00,0:01:00.87,Narr,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}He has never once\Nseen the second banana.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.70,0:01:04.16,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Papa, who’s that lady?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.25,0:01:06.08,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Mrs. Lusk. Walter’s wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.16,0:01:07.45,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}What’s her first name?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.79,0:01:08.79,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}It’s…
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.79,0:01:13.95,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Door, Teddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.37,0:01:28.25,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Oh — I’m fine, thank you.\NThe wall’s warm. From the ovens.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.29,0:01:30.87,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}It’s the small rye.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.70,0:01:33.50,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}…That was Walter’s.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.58,0:01:37.79,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Every day at four.\NHe’d tear the end off before he’d paid.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.87,0:01:39.58,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}That sign was for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.75,0:01:44.33,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}He stood by the lamp.\NLaughed before I even fell.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.41,0:01:47.08,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}He said you lean. Right before.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.16,0:01:49.41,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}He loved that you never fixed it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.70,0:01:53.25,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Thirty-one minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.79,0:01:57.04,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Walter climbed up every Sunday.\NSet it right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.12,0:01:59.04,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}It loses a minute a week.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.62,0:02:02.33,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}…Thirty-one Sundays.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.95,0:02:04.54,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}I don’t want it fixed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.62,0:02:06.00,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Isn’t that awful?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.08,0:02:07.08,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.16,0:02:10.04,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}The minister came twice.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.12,0:02:12.45,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Called me Ethel. Both times.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.33,0:02:15.00,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Well. He calls me Oscar, so—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.08,0:02:17.20,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Oh… you don’t have to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.66,0:02:20.33,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}I saw you. Every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.45,0:02:22.16,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}I didn’t know what to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.25,0:02:23.62,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Nobody does.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.75,0:02:27.58,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Mr. Bunce. No.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.37,0:02:34.62,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}There. Now we both\Nlook ridiculous, Mrs. Lusk.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.75,0:02:36.75,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Edith.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.41,0:02:38.41,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}…Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.20,0:02:41.20,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Edith.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.04,0:02:45.20,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Nobody’s said it since April.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.91,0:02:54.37,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}That’s yours.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.45,0:02:56.12,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}You eat too, Oswald.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.70,0:03:05.04,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}There’s the lean.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.33,0:03:12.91,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Papa! You’re letting the heat out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.00,0:03:13.91,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.29,0:03:17.70,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}What’s your first name?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.79,0:03:19.00,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}It’s Edith.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.08,0:03:20.95,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}I’m Teddy. I’m nearly nine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.04,0:03:22.66,Dlg,,0,0,248,,{\blur0.8}Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.87,0:03:26.20,Narr,,0,0,600,,{\blur0.8}This is Edith Lusk.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.29,0:03:29.16,Narr,,0,0,600,,{\blur0.8}She has lived here fifty-three years.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.66,0:03:31.45,Narr,,0,0,600,,{\blur0.8}She was in the first shot.
